   "x": 100,
   "w": 493,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Study profile"
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "y": 4138,
   "x": 673,
   "w": 667,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Reading notes"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 4164,
   "x": 100,
   "w": 493,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Who is behind the numbers?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 4164,
   "x": 673,
   "w": 667,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "What the report does—and does not—say."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4256,
   "x": 100,
   "w": 493,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The unit is a person–conversation record , not necessarily a unique individual. The 3,312 rows contain 1,456 unique user IDs, so some IDs contribute to more than one call."
  },
  {
   "tag": "b",
   "y": 4283,
   "x": 673,
   "w": 320,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Two complementary tables"
  },
  {
   "tag": "b",
   "y": 4283,
   "x": 1021,
   "w": 320,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Available-case denominators"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4306,
   "x": 673,
   "w": 320,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The people table supplies person-level ratings and demographics. The conversation table supplies pair averages. Every conversation has exactly two person rows."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4306,
   "x": 1021,
   "w": 320,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "End-affect pair averages are present for 1,603 of 1,656 conversations. Person-level change and enjoyment analyses use 3,257 nonmissing post-conversation records."
  },
  {
   "tag": "b",
   "y": 4366,
   "x": 115,
   "w": 135,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "32"
